hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15539","Sayyar ibn Hatim Abu Salamah al-Anazi narrated to us, he said: Jafar, meaning Ibn Sulayman, narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: I said to Abd al-Rahman ibn Khanbash al-Tamimi, and he was elderly, Did you meet the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes. He said: I said: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act on the night the devils sought to overpower him? And he said: The devils came down that night upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the valleys and the passes, and among them was a devil with a flame of fire in his hand, intending to burn thereby the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Jibril, peace be upon him, descended to him and said: O Muhammad, say. He said: What shall I say? He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created and spread and originated, and from the evil of what descends from the heaven, and from the evil of what ascends in it, and from the evil of the trials of night and day, and from the evil of every nocturnal comer except a comer who comes with good, O Merciful. He said: So their fire was extinguished, and Allah the Blessed and Exalted defeated them."
"15540","Affan narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us: Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, he said: A man asked Abd al-Rahman ibn Khanbash: How did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) act when the devils sought to overpower him? He said: The devils came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from the valleys and came down upon him from the mountains, and among them was a devil with a flame of fire, intending to burn thereby the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: So he was frightened, Jafar said: I think he said: He began to step back. He said: And Jibril, peace be upon him, came and said: O Muhammad, say. He said: What shall I say? He said: Say: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah, which no righteous nor wicked exceeds, from the evil of what He created and spread and originated, and from the evil of what descends from the heaven, and from the evil of what ascends in it, and from the evil of what He spread in the earth, and from the evil of what comes out of it, and from the evil of the trials of night and day, and from the evil of every nocturnal comer except a comer who comes with good, O Merciful. So the fire of the devils was extinguished, and Allah the Mighty and Majestic defeated them."
